Why this is here
----------------

An Illustrator plugin cannot be built without the Adobe Illustrator SDK, and
the resulting binary is not merely linked against it. Adobe ships the plugin
entry point, the message dispatch loop, and the suite acquisition as *source*,
in samplecode/common/, and every plugin compiles that source into itself. In a
release build of Enhanced Free Distort, seven of the twelve object files are
Adobe's:

    Main.obj  Plugin.obj  Suites.obj  AppContext.obj  SDKErrors.obj
    IAIUnicodeString.obj  SDKAboutPluginsHelper.obj

Each of those files carries Adobe's copyright and a license permitting use only
"in accordance with the terms of the Adobe license agreement accompanying it."
That is a restriction GPL section 10 forbids anyone from imposing on a recipient,
and section 5(c) requires the whole combined work to be licensed under the GPL,
which no one but Adobe is in a position to do for Adobe's code.

So the source in this repository is unambiguously GPL -- it contains no Adobe
code, and the SDK is referenced by path rather than vendored. The *compiled
plugin* would not be distributable under a bare GPL, because the license it
purported to grant would cover code the copyright holder has no authority to
relicense. Section 7 exists for exactly this situation, and this file uses it.

